\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ lib/pstack.fam — a program's network stack, set up: src/eth.fam's state from
\ the kernel's addresses (the program does no ARP of its own: the gateway's MAC
\ comes from the kernel, peers are learned from their frames), src/udp.fam's
\ sockets, and the dispatcher for the frames in the ring.
\
\   pstack ( slots -- )      pnetinit, netinfo, the ethernet and UDP state
\                            (TCP's is the program's: tcpinit when it listens)
\   pnetin ( buf len -- )    one frame from the ring: the sender learned, IPv4
\                            to ipin, UDP to udpin, TCP to tcpin, the rest dropped
\ Needs lib/pnet.fam src/eth.fam src/ip.fam src/udp.fam src/tcp.fam.
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

: pstack ( slots -- )
	pnetinit netinfo
	pinfo @ @ ipaddr !  pinfo @ 4 lit + @ ipmask !  pinfo @ 8 lit + @ ipgw !
	800 lit alloc txf !  80 lit alloc dup arpt ! 20 lit 0 lit do 0 lit over i 2 lit lshift + ! loop drop
	0 lit arpn !  8 lit alloc dup bcast ! 6 lit 0 lit do FF lit over i + c! loop drop
	ipgw @ pinfo @ C lit + arpadd
	udpinit ;

: pnetin ( buf len -- )
	over ethtype 800 lit = if
		over 1A lit + be32@ 2 lit pick 6 lit + arpadd
		E lit - swap E lit + swap ipin ?dup if dup 11 lit = if drop udpin else 6 lit = if tcpin else 2drop then then then
	else 2drop then ;
